.TH auto-set-lid-switch-mode 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-set-lid-switch-mode - Control response to laptop close

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-set-lid-switch-mode sleep-state
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
sleep-state ACPI S1|S2|S3|S4|S5|NONE|suspend|shutdown|none
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-set-lid-switch-mode
command controls the system response to the lid switch, i.e.
a laptop being closed.  The sleep-state argument may be any of
the standard ACPI states S1|S2|S3|S4|S5|NONE, or for convenience,
mnemonic states suspend|shutdown|none.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-set-lid-switch-mode suspend
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), acpi(4)

